          "returnType": null,
          "description": "Coordinates in target's own rendering layer — **not** a single fixed space. A hit inside the scene's UI layer reads in screen space (the same space RenderingContext.screenView maps into); a hit against the world tree reads in camera/world space (post pan/zoom/rotate — identical to screen space only at the default centered camera). This matches the space target.position/target.contains() already operate in for whichever layer target lives in, so the two always agree; it is deliberately not Pointer.x/Pointer.y, which is raw design-pixel space and does not track a panned or zoomed camera at all."
        },
